course: dictionary
lesson: 15335
title: Words for clothes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a thing you wear. A snowsuit is a noun, a naming word, for a warm outfit. The words around it give you clues. «Mia zipped up her snowsuit before she ran out to play in the snow.» Zipped and snow tell you it is clothing for cold weather.
explain: Look inside the word. Snowsuit is made of two smaller words: snow and suit. A suit here is a set of clothes that go together. So a snowsuit is a set of clothes for snow. Breaking a long word into parts is a good way to work out its meaning.
explain: Use the swap test. «Put on your snowsuit, it is freezing outside.» Could you put on a sandwich instead? No. Only clothing fits, so your meaning of snowsuit makes sense in the sentence.
explain: Clues can also tell you where or when something happens. «In Canada, many children wear a snowsuit to school in winter.» Winter and cold places are clues that a snowsuit is for keeping warm in very cold weather.
fact: A snowsuit is a warm, padded, waterproof outfit for playing in snow or cold weather.
fact: A snowsuit can be one piece, or it can be a jacket and trousers.
fact: In cold places such as Canada and the northern USA, children often wear snowsuits to school in winter.
fact: «Keep your snowsuit zipped up» helps you stay warm and avoid frostbite, which is damage to skin caused by freezing cold.
fact: Babies may wear snowsuits in a pushchair, but not in a car seat, because the padding can make the straps loose.
exercise: «Mia zipped up her snowsuit before she went out to play.» What is a snowsuit? | A hat with ear flaps | A sledge for going down hills | *A warm, padded, waterproof outfit for snow | A small bag for carrying snowballs
exercise: «Put on your snowsuit, it is freezing outside.» What kind of thing is a snowsuit? | *Clothing you wear | A game played in the playground | A type of weather | A food you eat for lunch
exercise: Ella's little brother sits in his pushchair in a snowsuit on a cold day. Why might a snowsuit be useful for him? | It makes him invisible | *It is warm and padded to keep him cosy | It is made of glass | It helps him run faster
test: «Children in Canada wear snowsuits to school in winter.» Find and copy one word that tells you where or when. | children | *winter | school | Canada
test: «Babies should not wear bulky snowsuits in car seats, because the straps can become loose.» Why? | Car seats are too big for snowsuits to fit | It makes the baby hungry | Snowsuits are too heavy to carry | *The padding can make the straps loose
exam: Jayden says, «A snowsuit is a kind of jumper.» Is he right? Why? | Yes, because it is worn on the top half of the body | No, a snowsuit is a warm, padded, waterproof outfit for snow and cold, which can be one piece or a jacket and trousers | No, because a snowsuit is a food | *Partly right, because a snowsuit is for keeping warm, so it does not matter what it is made of
